    "location": "html-block:74",
    "text": "Overview",
    "heading": "PowerLogic Energy Meters"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:75",
    "text": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:76",
    "text": "The PowerLogic Energy Meter combines highly accurate industrial grade split-core CTs and precision microprocessor based metering electronics to provide exceptional metering accuracy and greatly reduce the total metering system installed cost. Features:",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:77",
    "text": "High-resolution back-lit liquid crystal display",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:78",
    "text": "True reading display —No multipliers are required for data readings",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:79",
    "text": "High accuracy — ±1% systems accuracy from 2% to 100% of the CT rating meets ANSI C12.1 metering accuracy standards",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:80",
    "text": "kW demand metering — The optional EMCB also provides kW demand monitoring in the Energy Meter. The user can set the demand interval from five minutes to one hour to accurately measure kW demand.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:81",
    "text": "Simple, fast installation — Factory assembled split-core CTs reduce installation time and color coding makes determine correct phase matching easy.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:82",
    "text": "Easy integration to PowerLogic or Control/Data Acquisition Systems — Extended models have pulse output contacts, selectable from 1/10 to 1 kWh per pulse, for easy integration to existing control systems.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
    "location": "html-block:83",
    "text": "Automatic meter reading — The optional Energy Meter Communications Board (EMCB) provides serial Modbus RS-485 RTU communications for connecting the Energy Meter to a remote monitoring system. With the addition of the EMCB, the Energy Meter can be used with PowerLogic software for electrical cost allocation and billing of submetered electrical systems.",
    "heading": "Features"
  },
  {
